pproval coverage. 8.k.R preserves known warning-threshold failures even when required semantic services remain unavailable, without changing native reports, completion or unavailable-only unknown results. Real unchanged SRX graph rules find failures in unchanged artifacts after target or edge changes. Failed/unbound/incomplete dependency discovery never runs a falsely narrowed check; faulty check observations preserve native errors and actual scope. Coverage includes outside references, cyclic declared dependencies, unresolved real Git refs, early base guards, ambiguous/unused profiles, unexecuted empty scopes and owned snapshots without live freshness claims. All earlier behavior proofs and test identities are retained. 8.k.C extracts the same seed-selection and native validation/assessment/Core-lint blocks into two private helpers. A static AST extraction proof verifies the two substitutions and unchanged guards, reports, module bindings and profile behavior. All 285 existing test files and 9503 prior test IDs remain unchanged; targeted W/R regression rechecks behavior. No new semantics, error contracts, side effects or authority are introduced."
